"OLAYLAR_ORTACAG_IRAN_HINT_MAGRIB:0972-07-01:0":{"b": ["Hasan al-A'sam reoccupied Ramla and defeated a strong Fatimid army", "c3b5ad80"], "d": ["The Qarmatian leader Hasan al-A'sam reoccupied Ramla in Ramadan 361 (July 972) and defeated a strong Fatimid army; a year later he attacked Egypt by land and sea and besieged Cairo once more, but was defeated by al-Aziz Billah.", "f629e2e1"]},
"OLAYLAR_ORTACAG_IRAN_HINT_MAGRIB:0981-01-01:0":{"b": ["The Chinese envoy Wang Yande began traveling among the Uyghurs (981-984); his report is the main source on Turfan Uyghur culture.", "478d801b"], "d": ["The Chinese envoy Wang Yande began traveling among the Uyghurs (981-984); his report is the main source on Turfan Uyghur culture.", "478d801b"]},
"OLAYLAR_ORTACAG_IRAN_HINT_MAGRIB:0985-01-01:0":{"b": ["The army that Mansur b. Buluggin sent against Fez and Sijilmasa failed (374, 985).", "85a5064b"], "d": ["The army that Mansur b. Buluggin sent against Fez and Sijilmasa failed (374, 985).", "85a5064b"]},
"OLAYLAR_ORTACAG_IRAN_HINT_MAGRIB:0985-05-24:0":{"b": ["The Qarmatians of Bahrain occupied Kufa two years after Basra; they could not hold out against the Buyids and withdrew", "4b76d4b0"], "d": ["After the death of the Buyid Adud al-Dawla (372/983), the Qarmatians of Bahrain, wishing to display their strength in southern Iraq, attacked Basra in 373 (983-84) and made it pay tribute, and two years later they occupied Kufa; but they could not hold out against the Buyids and withdrew, and never again had a voice in Iraq.", "0451dba6"]},
